[226.344773, "o", "757-Try to avoid becoming too focussed on one \r\n758-issue, such as populated uniformity, as it may \r\n759-not lead you to the optimum decision. \r\n760-In order for the oven to be properly sized, the process \r\n761-speed defined below must be greater than the minimum \r\n762-calculated line speed. This will ensure that bottlenecks \r\n763-will not occur at the reflow oven. The process speed \r\n764-should be determined through testing or by the following \r\n765-equation: \r\n766-OVEN CHAMBER HEATED LENGTH PROCESS - \r\n767:SPEED - PROCESS DWELL TIME \r\n768-DEFINE PROCESS GAS \r\n769-If a nitrogen atmosphere is required for solderability or \r\n770-no-clean processing (see page lo), one needs to consider \r\n771-the purity required and the gas consumption. Be careful \r\n772-how the purity is measured, such that it is not measured \r\n773-at the gas inlet. \r\n774-REVIEW CONVEYOR DESIGN \r\n775-The conveying mechanism is perhaps the most over- \r\n776-looked aspect of equipment selection. One needs to \r\n"]
